WEBVTT

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.790
The genius who descended into 
the underworld, Akagi Shigeru.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.340
Soon, he would create legends there

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.970
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.970
<b>A True Outlaw</b>

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:21.520
as the man rumored to hail 
from the godly realm.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.160
Now that he's won his first game, 
the prelude to the legend,

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:29.600
the battle is about to 
move on to the next stage.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.410
Hi, over here.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.080
Sorry.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.110
This isn't really a 
place for kids your age,

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.780
but places like these are all I know.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:45.440
You can handle beer, right?

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.250
Let me tell you what's been set up.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.760
The match will be in three days, 
on Friday, at 8 PM.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.370
It'll be at a restaurant in 
the city called Sasagawa.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.380
The witness will be Miyauchi, 
the boss of the Takeyoshi group.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.050
He's the most chivalrous 
gambler in the Kanto region.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.830
Now, let's toast to our reunion.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.500
Before we do that,

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.010
tell me about the other condition.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.580
All right, let's discuss 
how we'll split the money.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.680
If we win this match, 
my cut will be 20%.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.590
The expenses for setting 
this up will eat about 10%.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.370
As the rep player, you get 20%.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.200
Nangou gets 50% as the one putting 
up the wager. That's standard.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.700
Why do people get so 
dirty as they get older?

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.300
You have nothing to lose, 
and you want 20%?

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.470
And 10% for the expenses 
sounds awfully high, too.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:52.590
I'm taking quite a few risks myself.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:56.320
If my superiors find out I'm doing this, 
I'll be facing a disciplinary dismissal.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:59.820
That's not enough of a risk.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.390
Damn, all right.

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.580
I'll give you 5% from my cut.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.190
That's not what I am talking about.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.800
I only have one condition.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.930
Let's start the wager at eight million.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.510
Eight million?!

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.310
Nangou only has six million!

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.170
Where are we going to get 
the other two million from?!

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.590
You're going to put it up.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.480
If you're not willing to risk 
even that, don't get involved.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.210
You damn brat!

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.530
If you don't accept, I'm out.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.220
All right, I'll accept!

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.490
Now you're a real corrupt cop.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.570
That's ridiculous!

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.110
That wager is insane!

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.500
Can't we at least limit it 
to the three million we won?

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.100
What's good about this is 
that it's not rational.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.360
Either way, we shouldn't lower 
the wager for this match.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.070
Doing that would be suicide.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.780
It's our insanity that they're afraid of.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:02.450
That night, I survived because 
I didn't hit the brakes.

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:04.200
That night?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.680
The game of chicken?

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:12.420
It was a gamble I made with some punks.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:17.090
That game was obviously 
rigged in their favor.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.410
First, they knew exactly 
where they needed to brake.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:26.720
Second, they chose the 
car on the right side.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:32.170
On the right side, they could jump out 
from the driver side door if necessary.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:36.010
The driver on the left can't do that,
since the other car blocks that side.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.070
Everything was rigged in their favor.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:42.250
In order for me to win,

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:46.710
I had to negate the condition 
that the game was based on.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.760
What condition?

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.760
That we didn't want to die.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.470
At the time, I wasn't afraid of dying.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:02.440
I had no intention of braking from the start.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.340
Obviously, the car shot off 
the cliff at full speed.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.240
Where those cliffs are situated,

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.220
the water suddenly gets 
deeper after a certain point.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:16.780
So braking actually lowers 
your chance of survival.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:20.190
But my opponent was too fixated on me,

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.990
missing his opportunity 
to jump from his car.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.590
He also braked.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.730
Of course, he bounced off the rocks 
before falling into the water.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.040
He ruined himself.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.230
Are you telling me I should 
do something like you did?

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.660
I can't do that!

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.560
Yes, you can.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:45.300
In fact, you already did.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.550
I'm sure you haven't forgotten.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:49.950
Back then,

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:51.790
when you were playing against Ryuuzaki,

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.590
the 5 of circles was a super dangerous tile.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.030
But...

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:10.140
That discard was akin to 
flooring it as you neared the cliff.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:17.200
Winning money you couldn't earn with 
30 years of honest work, or death?

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:21.050
That's not a bridge you could 
cross with a sane mind anyway.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.880
Nangou-san, throw yourself away.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.140
Just for one more night.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.990
With Yasuoka's additional two million,

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:37.500
the stakes in the match against 
the yakuza are now at eight million.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:42.120
Today, that would be equivalent 
to about 80 million yen,

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.070
all riding on this match.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.480
On the day of the match,

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:50.950
Akagi was summoned by the 
opponents he would be facing.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.960
Why do you have to go there 
just because they called you?

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:01.120
They're the kind of people who 
will kill for money, you know!

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.620
Akagi!

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:06.120
Well, there's also something 
I need to get from them.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.920
Listen, it's not too late.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:10.890
Let's call to cancel.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.760
I can't see any good coming of this.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.160
That doesn't matter.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.900
Tonight's Mahjong match will 
be a game of life or death.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.510
At this point, being locked up 
or threatened won't scare me.

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:25.310
But still... Akagi...

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.210
<b>Fuji Coffee</b>

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.210
This is it.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.070
What do you want to do?

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.120
If you're that worried, 
you can come in with me.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.400
No, I'm...

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.850
I'll come out when we're done.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.120
Should be about 30 minutes.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.960
Akagi...

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.270
We've been waiting for you, Akagi-san.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:07:59.590
This way, please.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.900
This is our second in command, Kurosaki.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.220
What is this place?

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.450
Pretty rotten customer base.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.460
They're all my underlings.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.300
You're surrounded.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.960
You're in a dark hole now.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.330
No matter what happens here...

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:29.440
You guys are always the same.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:33.770
You can't try to make 
deals by threatening me.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.280
Get it already!

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.900
I see.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:43.520
You're just as interesting 
as the rumors say you are.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:49.490
All right, I'll give it to you straight.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.510
Switch sides.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.360
That's the only option you have left.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:56.960
This isn't a threat.

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:01.970
The guy we have ready is a 
top player in this world.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:06.470
No matter how much of a genius 
you are, you will lose, 100%.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:10.320
If you back down now, 
we'll even accept your terms.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.710
This is your last chance.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:15.470
Terms, huh?

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.220
Okay then, half.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.710
Half of eight million?

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:22.020
So four million?

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.920
You're way off.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:30.060
The half I'm talking about is 
half of what your group is worth.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.690
I'm planning on ending you guys tonight,

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:39.220
so half of what is needed 
to ruin your group.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.970
I figure that's about 50 million.

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:45.840
If you're willing to hand 
that over, I'll consider it.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:51.240
Oh boy, I thought you were 
a little smarter than that.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.850
Fine then, we'll do it 
until one of us is crushed.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.570
But you're going to die.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.590
Are you aware of that?

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:03.090
Right back at you.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:05.450
There's no talking to you.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.050
Guess the deal's off.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:08.920
Then, I'm outta here.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.100
Do you have what you promised?

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.930
Aren't you in middle school?

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:21.850
What do you need that for?

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.000
I'm involved in a bit of a conflict.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:29.850
These are so useful, especially for 
making people drop their tough acts.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:34.360
When faced with this, 
they all stop acting.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:35.950
See ya.

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:50.110
So that's what you look like.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:53.580
You're my opponent for tonight, right?

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.810
How did you know?!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.450
He's completely different from you.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.820
Just around him, the air is colder.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:05.820
It's almost like a fish wandered 
into a pack of beasts.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:18.570
Let's see how real your 
expressionless face really is.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:21.940
The chance is one in five.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.340
You damn brat!

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:25.540
Wait, just watch.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:45.930
Seven to the right.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.980
That's the number of times the 
chamber rotated after you put in the bullet.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.540
When the center chamber is loaded,

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:55.470
considering the chamber rotates 
once with every trigger pull,

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:59.210
it will fire on the fourth, 
ninth, and fourteenth time.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:04.950
Even an amateur could tell the chamber 
rotated between four and nine times.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:08.950
You pulled the trigger knowing that.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.990
At first glance, it looked reckless, 
but it was all calculated.

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:20.530
You might be able to scare normal 
people shitless, but it won't work on me.

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:26.030
Fun.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:30.820
You're right, this guy is actually 
in a different league than Yagi.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.310
I'm looking forward to tonight.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.540
I wonder about that.

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:40.050
We don't know if you will 
survive until tonight.

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:43.050
We're only half done here.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.420
Am I wrong?

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:48.100
You pointed the gun at me 
and pulled the trigger.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:51.160
Therefore, you must do 
the same with yourself.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:55.390
Only then can we say this is over.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.900
Am I wrong, Akagi-kun?

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:01.390
I see.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:05.390
Do as you wish.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.990
But you will be pulling the trigger.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:10.140
Then it's truly an eye for an eye.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.710
Ichikawa!

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:14.150
Don't do something stupid 
because the kid taunted you!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.680
In this world, the more stupid,

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:21.850
the more insane things are, 
the more fun they are.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:27.320
You...

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.560
Yes. I am blind.

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:36.010
When I was young, 
I played a game like this.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:40.070
The gun misfired and I lost my sight.

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:42.570
There you are.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.180
Sorry, you'll have to be patient with me.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:53.080
I can't aim without doing this.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:55.430
But now, it's fine.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:58.150
If the gun fires, 
you'll be going straight to Hell.

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:01.890
How do you feel, Akagi-kun?

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.940
This is fun...

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.700
The more insane things are, 
the more fun they are.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:09.980
Stop it, Ichikawa!

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.950
What if it actually fires—

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:12.870
It won't!

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.700
How could it?

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:20.360
Do you think it's this kid's 
fate to die here in vain?

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.210
No, that won't happen!

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:27.180
Fate says that it won't fire!

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:37.060
His fate doesn't allow him to die here.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.770
Yeah, right.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:42.320
You said it earlier yourself.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.830
The chamber rotated seven times.

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:48.180
So it would work for another turn.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.440
Your hearing is your lifeline.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:54.010
There's no way that you would mishear.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:57.190
You don't believe in luck or fate.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.680
What you believe in is your own ears.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.800
Only your own, superior ability.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:04.560
Am I wrong?

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.840
To be honest, I'm like that, too.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:20.800
Akagi!

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.190
Are you okay?

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:25.690
Yeah, not a scratch on me, see?

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.500
Y-Yeah...

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.180
Whew, that's a relief.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:37.360
One of my kind?

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:42.420
<i>No, there's no one like me.</i>

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:45.190
Akagi?

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:49.550
<i>Him or me... one of us is the fake.</i>

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.140
<i>The fake outlaw.</i>

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:59.240
<b>Restaurant Sasagawa</b>

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:05.240
<b>Boss of the Takeyoshi Group</b>

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:05.240
<b>Miyauchi</b>

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:05.240
The witness, Miyauchi, 
boss of the Takeyoshi Group, arrives.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:07.710
He's late.

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:12.250
What's Akagi doing?!

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.920
It's about to begin!

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:15.200
That's weird.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:19.990
Everything seemed fine when the 
Kawada group summoned him earlier.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.500
Could he have been kidnapped by them?!

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.980
N-No way!

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:44.680
I'm surprised you actually came.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.420
I'm glad you came.

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:52.420
I really am!

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:58.310
Hey, not the head!

00:16:58.310 --> 00:16:59.550
He'll die!

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:04.270
Who gives a shit if this asshole dies?

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:09.870
Do you know what happened to Takeru?

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:11.800
Who?

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.880
The one you played chicken with.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:21.120
He barely survived, but they don't 
know if he will ever fully recover.

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:24.350
One mistake and that 
would have been me.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:27.850
You're so damn cocky!

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:31.340
I bet you think we won't 
do anything serious to you.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.960
Unfortunately, you thought wrong!

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:36.370
If you die, I'll worry about it then!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.540
I'm still a minor.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:42.000
Killing someone won't mean anything.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:45.650
Come on, kid, fight me!

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:47.610
It's not enough.

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:53.080
Even as a minor, killing three 
people will have consequences.

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:58.150
I need enough injuries so I can 
claim I acted in self defense.

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.120
What did you just say?

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:03.540
Well? What did you say?!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:06.160
What did you say?!

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:09.480
You little shit!

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:10.870
Die!

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:11.700
Stop it!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.450
You have to apologize!

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.090
You don't know what he'll do if he snaps!

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.340
Apologize!

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:24.360
Let's kill this asshole!

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:38.660
What is that?!

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:39.560
It's a gun!

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:40.130
A gun!

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.990
Did you come to again?

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.990
Saying "Let's kill this asshole!"

00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:09.690
means you won't mind if 
you get killed yourself.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:11.360
Right?

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.170
Stop, please stop!

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:15.880
Don't move.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.730
My finger is on the trigger.

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:23.470
When I was a kid, I squished a bug.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:26.400
I feel the same now as I did then.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:33.410
S-Sto—

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:36.750
Not enough.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:52.460
Get out of here.

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:55.300
You piss me off.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.890
I'll kill you.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.820
I'm not going to put myself at 
risk for little idiots like you.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:17.320
I only put two bullets in to begin with.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:19.510
Fake anger.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:20.950
Fake words.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.190
Fake fights.

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.700
I'm sick of all that.

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:29.310
Those kinds of games 
will never be enough me.

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:31.770
They will never satisfy my soul.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:35.050
<i>The match is on Friday at 8 PM.</i>

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:37.770
<i>It'll be at a restaurant in 
Akasaka called Sasagawa.</i>

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.120
I guess I'll go...

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:55.140
...to walk the true line between 
life and death once more.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:59.020
This is what happened 
on the day of the match.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:03.230
But it was nothing but a side show.

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:07.700
Akagi would experience a true 
fight to the death that night...

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:19.780
Next time: "The Treacherous Tse Ii Men."

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:20.550
